<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aurora de Chile</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1812">1812</a>–<a href="/years/1813">1813</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aurora de Chile was the first newspaper published in Chile, issued weekly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santiago">Santiago</a> from February 1812 to April 1813 on a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> press brought from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. Edited by the priest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camilo-henriquez">Camilo Henríquez</a> under the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-miguel-carrera">José Miguel Carrera</a>, it spread the ideas of independence and popular <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>. It was succeeded by El Monitor Araucano.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aurora-de-chile.jpg" alt="Aurora de Chile" width="320" height="485" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Auroradechile-01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
